  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "If rose bushes are spaced about \\(1\\) foot apart, approximately how many bushes are needed to surround a circular patio whose radius is \\(12\\) feet?",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(12\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(38\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(48\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(75\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(450\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-1988-p13.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The bushes surround the circular edge, so their number is about the circumference \\(2\\pi r = 2\\pi(12).\\)\n\nUsing \\(\\pi \\approx 3.14,\\) this is about \\(2 \\times 3.14 \\times 12 \\approx 75\\) feet, so roughly \\(75\\) bushes are needed.\n\nThus, the correct answer is D .",
      "hints": [
        "The bushes go around the edge, so find the circumference \\(2\\pi r\\)",
        "With \\(\\pi \\approx 3.14,\\) compute \\(2 \\times 3.14 \\times 12\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
